1. 1. Can you explain the difference between composition and inheritance?
When would you prefer one over the other?

Inheritance: Child class inherits behavior from parent class using extends. 
Used for is-a relationship
Example: class Dog extends Animal

Composition: Class contains objects of other classes as fields. 
Used for has-a relationship.
Example: class Car { Engine engine; }

When to prefer:
composition — it gives flexibility and reduces tight coupling.
Use inheritance only when subclass truly “is a” parent (behaviorally).

