2. What are the key principles of OOP, 
and how do you ensure they’re applied effectively in large codebases?

Encapsulation – Hide internal data; expose through getters/setters
Abstraction – Hide complexity; expose only required functionality.
Inheritance – Reuse behavior from base class.
Polymorphism – Same method behaves differently (overriding).

As a tech lead: enforce via design reviews, interfaces, 
and clean class boundaries to reduce coupling.

