3.Explain how hashCode() and equals() work together.
 What could happen if they are not implemented properly?
 
If two objects are equal (equals() returns true), they must have the same hashCode().
If not followed → inconsistent behavior in HashMap, HashSet, etc. (e.g., missing elements).

Best practice:
Use Objects.hash() or @EqualsAndHashCode (Lombok) to ensure correctness. 

