4. Why is String immutable in Java? What are the advantages and possible drawbacks of this design?

Security: prevents modification of sensitive data (e.g., URLs, file paths).
Thread Safety: shared safely across threads.
Hashing: used as keys in HashMap; immutability ensures consistent hash.
Performance: String Pool optimization.

Drawback: Frequent concatenation creates new objects (use StringBuilder instead).

