7. What are final, finally, and finalize() — and how are they different?

final - “you can’t change or override this” after it’s created
can't change final variable, can't override final method, can't extend final class.

finally - block of code that always runs, no matter what happens — success, failure, or exception.

finalize() - method in the Object class that is called by the Garbage Collector (GC) 
before destroying an object.
it’s deprecated now in modern Java — replaced by better tools like try-catch,cleaner resources

