9. Can you explain how Java handles parameter passing — is it by value or by reference?

Java is always pass-by-value.

For primitives → copies the value.

For objects → copies the reference (so both refer to same object).

-----

10. What’s the difference between a shallow copy and a deep copy? How would you implement deep copy? 

Shallow copy: Copies fields as-is (shared object references).

Deep copy: Recursively copies entire object graph.

When deep copy? — when mutable objects are referenced inside another object.

Employee e2 = new Employee(e1); // shallow copy
Employee e3 = SerializationUtils.clone(e1); // deep copy


